<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        Grants what a running user needs to invoke the Cloudflare_Turnstile Named Credential.
        Modelled line-for-line on SharePoint_Integration_Access; read that file's header too.

        🔴 THIS SET WILL NOT DEPLOY UNTIL "Turnstile_Credential" EXISTS IN THE ORG.
        externalCredentialPrincipalAccesses below references "Turnstile_Credential-
        Turnstile_Principal" BY NAME. Unlike SharePoint_Credential, this External Credential IS
        shipped as metadata (externalCredentials/Turnstile_Credential.externalCredential-meta.xml)
        and its shape was proven against this org on 2026-08-30 — so "deploy the credential first,
        or in the same payload" is the whole dependency, not a manual Setup step.

        🔴 BOTH GRANTS BELOW ARE LOAD-BEARING, AND THE FAILURE THEY PREVENT WAS MEASURED HERE.
        Without them a callout on this Named Credential throws, BEFORE the request is sent:
            System.CalloutException: We couldn't access the credential(s). You might not have the
            required permissions, or the external credential "Turnstile_Credential" might not exist.
        Measured on usman-dpeg 2026-08-30 as a System Administrator with no assignment — note that
        the System Administrator profile does NOT carry this implicitly. The message names a
        missing credential as its first hypothesis, which sends a diagnosis down the wrong path;
        the credential existed, the grant did not.

        UserExternalCredential object read is REQUIRED TO USE ANY Named Credential at all —
        precedent: Broker_Protection_Access carries the identical grant with the identical
        justification ("without object read on UserExternalCredential the callout throws before
        sending", found via debug log 2026-08-01 on this same org). Do not omit it.

        ═══ 🔴 WHO THIS MUST BE ASSIGNED TO: THE SITE GUEST USER ═══
        The only production caller is BrokerPortalService.submitDeal, which runs as the DPEG Broker
        Portal LWR site's GUEST user. Guest-user permissioning cannot be done through the profile —
        profiles/** is force-ignored (.forceignore line 28), so every profile entry in this repo is
        inert fiction. Assign this set to the guest user by hand:
            Setup > Digital Experiences > All Sites > DPEG Broker Portal > Workspaces > Administration
            > Pages > Public Access Settings > (guest profile page) > View Users > the guest user
            > Permission Set Assignments > Edit > add "Turnstile Integration Access".
        ⚠ Permission set ASSIGNMENT is not deployable metadata. A green deploy of this file grants
        nothing on its own. The acceptance test is a browser submission on the live guest page — a
        deploy result cannot substitute for it (design-requirements.md §0 GATE C).

        ═══ NO fieldPermissions, NO classAccesses, DELIBERATELY ═══
        There is no new field in WS4. There is no new Apex ENTRY POINT either: Apex class access is
        enforced at entry points only (@AuraEnabled / REST / VF), and the guest's entry point is
        BrokerPortalController.submitDeal, which is already reachable today.
        TurnstileVerificationService is called internally from BrokerPortalService and needs no
        grant of its own. Keeping this file at zero fieldPermissions also means the REPLACE-not-
        merge permission-set-deploy hazard (ARCHITECTURE.md §2 Standards) has nothing here to
        destroy on a future redeploy.
    -->
    <description>Grants External Credential Principal Access to Turnstile_Credential plus UserExternalCredential read, required to invoke the Cloudflare Turnstile Named Credential. Assign to the DPEG Broker Portal site guest user. See ARCHITECTURE.md 3.5.</description>
    <externalCredentialPrincipalAccesses>
        <enabled>true</enabled>
        <externalCredentialPrincipal>Turnstile_Credential-Turnstile_Principal</externalCredentialPrincipal>
    </externalCredentialPrincipalAccesses>
    <hasActivationRequired>false</hasActivationRequired>
    <label>Turnstile Integration Access</label>
    <objectPermissions>
        <allowCreate>false</allowCreate>
        <allowDelete>false</allowDelete>
        <allowEdit>false</allowEdit>
        <allowRead>true</allowRead>
        <modifyAllRecords>false</modifyAllRecords>
        <object>UserExternalCredential</object>
        <viewAllRecords>false</viewAllRecords>
    </objectPermissions>
</PermissionSet>
